    "overall_comment": "The translation broadly preserves the line-by-line dialogue and most scientific reasoning, with correct numerical relations and notation. However, quality is seriously weakened by terminology errors, especially translating “wave function” as “ತರಂಗ ಉತ್ಪನ್ನ” (“wave product”) and using “ವ್ಯಾಪ್ತಿ” where amplitude is intended. There are also malformed and mixed-script text such as “ಲ್ಯూique,” duplicated “ಸರಿ.ಸರಿ.,” an Arabic insertion (“بالکل”), and several awkward or nonstandard word choices. These issues make the Kannada less natural and occasionally alter technical meaning."
